---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import {designs} from '../data/jhula/designs';
import {setDirections} from '../data/jhula/sets';
const groups=['01-03','04-06','07-09','10-12'];
---
<Shell title="Odia Poetry Jhula" description="A little of home, wherever words take you. Explore twelve Jhula designs and their matching Poetry Kits, then help choose the first samples." active="explore" wide related={false} shareImage={{src:'/images/poetry-jhula/story-v2.png',alt:'Imagined scene of a woman writing and a man reading with their Jhulas nearby',width:1536,height:1024}}>
<article class="jhula wrap">
<header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">ODIA POETRY JHULA · A STORY IN CLOTH</p><h1>Some things carry<br/><em>more than words.</em></h1><p class="lead">A familiar book. An unfinished poem.<br/>A little of home, wherever we go.</p><p>For women and men who read, write, listen and remember. Twelve Jhulas, each imagined with a matching set of everyday companions.</p><nav aria-label="On this page"><a href="#story">Read the story ↓</a><a href="#collection">Explore all twelve ↓</a><a href="#vote">Help us choose ↓</a></nav><figure><img src="/images/poetry-jhula/story-v2.png" width="1536" height="1024" alt="Imagined scene of a woman writing beside a man reading, with soft cloth Jhulas resting near their chairs" fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>An imagined moment between readers · AI-created story and product imagery.</figcaption></figure></header>
<div class="specs"><span>Tussar + khadi directions</span><span>90 cm finished sling</span><span>Wooden button + cloth loop</span><span>12 unique designs</span></div>
<section id="story" class="poetic-story wrap"><p class="eyebrow">AN IMAGINED DAY · ORIGINAL WORDS FOR THIS COLLECTION</p><div class="story-intro"><h2>Two readers.<br/>A thousand <em>quiet journeys.</em></h2><p class="lead">The day begins before either of them has found the right words.</p></div><div class="chapters"><article><span>01 / MORNING</span><h3>A page goes with her.</h3><p>She slips a book into her Jhula, beside the notebook where a poem is still becoming. Across town, he pauses over a line he remembers from home, then puts his pen away.</p><p>The wooden button closes.<br/>The morning opens.</p></article><article><span>02 / ON THE WAY</span><h3>A little of home travels.</h3><p>Her sari brushes the cloth at her side. His Jhula rests against an everyday kurta. Between errands and conversations, each finds a moment to read, a sentence to keep.</p><p>Somewhere beyond Odisha, someone opens an Odia book—and a familiar voice returns.</p></article><article><span>03 / EVENING</span><h3>A poem finds company.</h3><p>By evening, they share a table. She reads a few lines. He listens, then offers a page of his own. A bookmark changes books. A thought finds its way into the margin.</p><p>The bags rest beside their chairs.<br/>There is more to carry home.</p></article></div><blockquote>“Let the cloth carry the book.<br/>Let the book carry a voice.<br/>Let the voice find <em>someone listening.</em>”</blockquote><div class="story-purpose"><p>We imagine the Jhula as part of a poet’s everyday attire: soft cloth, an unhurried silhouette, room for a book and a thought. A sari, a kurta, whatever feels like you. Every design belongs to whoever chooses it.</p><p>Rooted in Odisha’s textile vocabulary, this collection hopes to connect readers, writers and local makers. Paid craft work, writer visibility and creator income are the purpose; materials, partnerships and payment terms will need to be agreed before production.</p></div></section>
<section id="kit"><p class="eyebrow">THE POETRY KIT</p><h2>One thread.<br/><em>Six companions.</em></h2><p class="lead">The same border finds another page.<br/>The same colour keeps a pen company.</p><p>Each Jhula has its own matching Poetry Kit: the bag, an A5 cloth notebook, a refillable pen, a bookmark, a pen sleeve and an Odia poetry book to be selected. Its colour and border connect the everyday things we carry.</p><p>We intend to pay and credit makers and creators. Actual materials, partnerships, book selection and payment terms remain to be agreed.</p></section>
<section id="collection"><p class="eyebrow">TWELVE DESIGNS · TWELVE MATCHING SETS</p><h2>Find the one that <em>feels like you.</em></h2><p>See all twelve matching sets and open any original bag view. Rate as many designs as you like, add comments, and choose a favourite. Save your response at the end of this page.</p><p class="note">All images are AI-generated concepts awaiting physical sampling. The sling specification is <strong>90 cm along the exposed strap between its top attachment points</strong>, not the vertical drop. Set images interpret the bags; the original bag views remain the design reference.</p>
<div class="designs">{designs.map((d,i)=>{const x=(i%3)*512;const [bx,by,bw,bh]=d.view.split(' ');return <article class="design" id={'design-'+d.id}><div class="design-title"><p class="eyebrow">{d.id} · {d.family==='Core'?'The originals':d.family}</p><h3>{d.name}</h3></div><svg viewBox={x+' 0 512 1024'} role="img" aria-label={d.name+' matching Poetry Kit concept'}><defs><clipPath id={'set-'+d.id}><rect x={x} y="0" width="512" height="1024"/></clipPath></defs><image clip-path={'url(#set-'+d.id+')'} href={'/images/poetry-jhula/sets-'+groups[Math.floor(i/3)]+'-v2.png'} width="1536" height="1024"/></svg><div class="design-copy"><p class="set-line">{setDirections[d.id].line}</p><p>{setDirections[d.id].detail}</p><details><summary>View the original Jhula</summary><svg viewBox={d.view} role="img" aria-label={d.name+' original bag concept'}><defs><clipPath id={'bag-'+d.id}><rect x={bx} y={by} width={bw} height={bh}/></clipPath></defs><image clip-path={'url(#bag-'+d.id+')'} href={d.src} width={d.imageWidth} height={d.imageHeight}/></svg><p>{d.detail}</p><p><strong>Cloth direction:</strong> {d.material}</p></details><fieldset class="design-feedback" data-feedback-fields disabled><legend>Your view of {d.name}</legend><fieldset class="rating-scale"><legend>Rating <span>(optional)</span></legend><div class="rating-options">{[1,2,3,4,5].map(n=><label><input type="radio" form="jhula-feedback" name={'rating-'+d.id} value={n} aria-label={n+' out of 5 for '+d.name}/><span>{n} ★</span></label>)}</div><p class="rating-hint">1 · Not for me &nbsp; 5 · Love it</p><button type="button" class="clear-rating" data-clear-rating={d.id}>Clear rating</button></fieldset><label class="favourite-option"><input type="radio" form="jhula-feedback" name="favourite" value={d.id}/> My favourite design</label><label class="design-comment">Comment on this design <span>(optional)</span><textarea form="jhula-feedback" name={'comment-'+d.id} maxlength="300" rows="3" placeholder="Colour, cloth, shape, or something you would change…"></textarea></label></fieldset></div></article>})}</div></section>
<section class="styling"><p class="eyebrow">EVERYDAY POETIC ATTIRE</p><h2>A sari. A kurta.<br/><em>Whatever feels like you.</em></h2><p>The same collection belongs to whoever chooses it. Soft cloth and a familiar book can find their place in an ordinary day.</p><figure><img src="/images/poetry-jhula/women-styling.png" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" alt="AI styling concept showing women carrying Jhulas with a green sari and an ivory kurta"/><figcaption>Styling concept only; loaded samples will establish actual fit and comfort.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section id="vote" class="vote"><p class="eyebrow">NOW, A LITTLE SPACE FOR YOUR VOICE</p><h2>The next page<br/><em>is yours.</em></h2><p class="lead">Which Jhula would you carry?</p><p>Rate at least one design above, or as many as you like. A favourite and all comments are optional. Your ratings and comments are private feedback for the project team.</p>
<form id="jhula-feedback" data-endpoint="https://odia-kabira-jhula.aquera-1216.chatgpt.site/api/ratings">
<fieldset data-feedback-fields disabled><legend>A few final thoughts</legend><label class="form-field">Your name <span>(optional)</span><input name="name" maxlength="80" autocomplete="name"/></label><fieldset class="kit-preference"><legend>What would you prefer?</legend>{[['bag','Just the Jhula'],['kit','The Poetry Kit'],['unsure','Not sure yet']].map(([value,label])=><label><input type="radio" name="kit" value={value} checked={value==='unsure'}/>{label}</label>)}</fieldset><label class="form-field">Overall comment <span>(optional · up to 1,000 characters)</span><textarea name="comment" maxlength="1000" rows="5" placeholder="What would make these designs more useful or meaningful to you?"></textarea></label><p id="rating-summary" aria-live="polite">No designs rated yet.</p><button type="button" id="clear-favourite" class="clear-rating">Clear favourite choice</button><p class="note">Save once, then update your response here whenever you wish. This is a design survey, not an order or preorder.</p><button class="vote-button" type="submit" id="save-ratings">Save ratings & comments</button></fieldset>
<p id="ratings-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Connecting to saved responses…</p><p id="ratings-error" role="alert" hidden></p><button type="button" id="retry-ratings" hidden>Retry loading saved response</button><div id="withdraw-area" hidden><button type="button" id="withdraw-ratings">Withdraw my saved response</button><div id="withdraw-confirm" hidden><p>Remove your saved ratings and comments? This cannot be undone.</p><button type="button" id="confirm-withdraw">Yes, withdraw my response</button><button type="button" id="cancel-withdraw">Keep my response</button></div></div>
<noscript><p>Enable JavaScript to save ratings and comments on this page.</p></noscript>
</form>
<details class="ratings-privacy"><summary>How your feedback is saved</summary><p>The project team can review your ratings, favourite, kit preference, optional name, comments and submission times. They are not displayed publicly. Please avoid sensitive personal information.</p><p>A random response key is stored in this browser on Project Odisha so you can revise or withdraw your response here. The server stores only a hash of that key. Clearing browser storage or switching devices may create a separate response and prevent access to the earlier one. This is an informal survey, not verified one-person-one-vote.</p><p>Responses are saved through our existing survey service while you stay on this page. Earlier shortlist votes remain preserved separately; they are not automatically combined with these new ratings.</p></details></section>

<details class="credits"><summary>About the concepts and craft inspiration</summary><p>Contemporary original concept studies inspired by Odisha’s textile vocabulary, not verified historical reproductions or certified craft products. No maker partnership or finished product is claimed.</p><p>Puri directions draw on Pipili appliqué and Raghurajpur painting. Katak linework translates Tarakasi into proposed embroidery, not silver. Western Odisha studies start with Sambalpur–Bargarh weaving references and do not represent every regional tradition.</p><p>All product and styling images were AI-generated for this collection. Books are placeholders; title and edition remain unselected. Fabric, dimensions, colourfastness, construction, fit and price need physical sampling.</p><p>Craft background: <a href="https://odishatourism.gov.in/en/arts-crafts-handloom">Odisha Tourism</a> · <a href="https://eodbodisha.odisha.gov.in/Upload/ODOP/Prod_Desc/Sambalpur.pdf">Sambalpur district profile</a>.</p></details>
<p class="return"><a href="/literature/">Continue into Odia literature →</a></p>
</article>
</Shell>
<script>
import '../scripts/jhula-feedback';
</script>
<style>
.jhula{padding-bottom:70px}.jhula section{padding-block:52px;scroll-margin-top:110px}.hero{display:block;padding-top:45px}.hero h1{font-size:clamp(44px,7vw,100px);line-height:1.07;margin:20px 0 28px;max-width:1000px}.jhula h2{font-size:clamp(32px,4vw,58px);line-height:1.15}.jhula h3{font-size:28px;line-height:1.2}.jhula em{color:var(--sea)}.jhula p{line-height:1.8;max-width:920px}.lead{font-size:clamp(21px,2.3vw,28px)}.hero>p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:760px}.hero nav{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:14px 30px;margin:25px 0}.hero nav a,.return a{padding:12px 0;min-height:44px}.jhula figure{margin:30px 0 0}.jhula figure img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}.hero figure img{max-height:700px;object-fit:cover}.jhula figcaption,.note{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted)}.jhula figcaption{padding-top:12px}.specs{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px 28px;border-block:1px solid var(--line);padding:20px 0;margin-top:30px;font-size:14px}.chapters{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:35px}.chapters article>span{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:var(--earth)}.chapters h3{font-size:30px}.poetic-story blockquote{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:clamp(26px,3.7vw,48px);line-height:1.6;text-align:center;margin:60px 0}.story-purpose{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:36px}#kit{border-block:1px solid var(--line)}.designs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:25px;margin-top:32px}.design{border:1px solid var(--line);background:var(--paper);min-width:0}.design-title,.design-copy{padding:20px}.design-title h3{margin:10px 0 0}.design-title{min-height:120px}.design>svg{width:100%;height:430px;display:block;background:#eee8dd}.design-copy>p{font-size:15px}.set-line{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:21px!important}.design details{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:14px}.design summary,.credits summary{cursor:pointer;padding:12px 0;min-height:44px}.design details svg{width:100%;height:370px}.design details p{font-size:14px}.styling{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.vote{max-width:900px;margin:auto}.vote-button{display:inline-block;background:var(--sea);color:white;padding:18px 26px;text-decoration:none;margin:18px 0;font-weight:600}.credits{border-block:1px solid var(--line);padding:15px 0}.jhula a:focus-visible,.jhula summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--earth);outline-offset:5px}@media(max-width:900px){.designs{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}.chapters{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:20px}.story-purpose{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:0}.hero figure img{max-height:none}}@media(max-width:550px){.jhula section{padding-block:34px}.designs{grid-template-columns:1fr}.design-title{min-height:0}.design>svg{height:500px}.hero{padding-top:25px}.hero nav{gap:8px 20px}.poetic-story blockquote{margin:35px 0}.specs{font-size:12px;gap:10px 18px}}

.design-feedback{margin:22px 0 0;padding:18px 0 0;border:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);min-width:0}.design-feedback>legend{font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:21px;padding-top:15px}.rating-scale{border:0;padding:10px 0;margin:0;min-width:0}.rating-scale legend{font-size:15px}.rating-options{display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:10px}.rating-options label{position:relative;cursor:pointer}.rating-options input{position:absolute;opacity:0;width:1px;height:1px}.rating-options span{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;min-width:44px;min-height:44px;padding:5px;border:1px solid var(--sea);border-radius:3px;color:var(--sea);font-size:15px}.rating-options input:checked+span{background:var(--sea);color:#fff}.rating-options input:focus-visible+span{outline:3px solid var(--earth);outline-offset:3px}.rating-hint{font-size:12px!important;margin:7px 0}.clear-rating{background:none;border:0;text-decoration:underline;color:var(--sea);cursor:pointer;padding:10px 0;min-height:44px}.favourite-option{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;padding:12px 0;min-height:44px;font-size:15px}.favourite-option input,.kit-preference input{width:19px;height:19px;accent-color:var(--sea);flex-shrink:0}.design-comment{display:block;font-size:15px}.design-comment span,.form-field span,.rating-scale legend span{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}.design-comment textarea,.form-field textarea,.form-field input{display:block;width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;background:#fffdf8;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:3px;padding:12px;font:inherit;margin-top:9px;resize:vertical}.design-feedback:disabled{opacity:.65}#jhula-feedback>fieldset{border:0;padding:0;min-width:0}#jhula-feedback>fieldset>legend{font-size:24px;font-family:Georgia,serif;margin-bottom:24px}.form-field{display:block;margin:20px 0}.kit-preference{border:1px solid var(--line);padding:18px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:16px}.kit-preference label{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;min-height:44px}#save-ratings{border:0;cursor:pointer;font:inherit}#save-ratings:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:wait}#ratings-error{padding:15px;border-left:3px solid #9b3624;color:#842817;background:#fff2ed}#ratings-status{font-weight:600}#retry-ratings,#withdraw-ratings,#confirm-withdraw,#cancel-withdraw{padding:12px 18px;min-height:44px;margin:8px 10px 8px 0;border:1px solid var(--sea);background:transparent;color:var(--sea);cursor:pointer}#withdraw-confirm{padding:16px;background:var(--paper)}.ratings-privacy{margin-top:24px}.ratings-privacy summary{cursor:pointer;min-height:44px;padding:12px 0}.ratings-privacy p{font-size:14px}.vote fieldset:disabled{opacity:.65}
</style>
